    "turn_text": "well as as as regards the the report by my if the rule said you're supposed to release the report that i'd be for releasing it but that's not what the rules that the rules that one someone has left congress you're not supposed to release those reports and that's something we did that's the rules now unfortunately have people in this town who don't want to follow the rules But to me, it's like if the rules dictate a certain course of action, we should follow the rules. You have them for, you don't have rules, you don't have the, I mean, you have the, I said this, the Constitution is for those difficult times. That's when it matters most. And the same with rules that you've had in place for years, they matter most when it's a difficult situation. So I would just say follow the rules. And again, if the rules said something different, I would be for follows the rules. But you have some who say, no, no, break the rules in this situation, because we don't like the particular nominee who's been put forward by the president, who, after all, who, by the way, won in a landslide, won with a mandate from the people. But no, no, no, we got to break the rules, because we can't have him getting his nominee in the position he wants it.",
